  "id": "COMPOUND:24672 - PROTEIN:5802",
  "verbalization": "(+)-Isoitalicene is implicated in the regulation of Hs746T through a series of molecular interactions that involve the mitochondrial thioredoxin protein. This relationship is supported by the evidence that (+)-Isoitalicene acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Spathelia bischromene and Diplotrin A, which in turn target Hs746T. The shared target of these compounds with thioredoxin, mitochondrial suggests a potential mechanism by which (+)-Isoitalicene may influence Hs746T through the modulation of thioredoxin activity. The presence of multiple pathways converging on thioredoxin, mitochondrial, and ultimately Hs746T highlights a possible role for thioredoxin in mediating the effects of (+)-Isoitalicene. The integration of these pathways underscores the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the importance of thioredoxin as a central node in the network of interactions linking (+)-Isoitalicene to Hs746T.",
